{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/662744-futile-proposition-by-night-studios","id":662744,"title":"Futile Proposition: By Night Studios","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-13T00:06:18-07:00","id":662744,"title":"Futile Proposition: By Night Studios","content":"Even though I'm certain its a futile proposition, does anybody know what would be involved in petitioning White Wolf to revoke the licensing from this company? Or even if they'd listen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/494-exalted-viovode","name":"Exalted Viovode","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T00:41:00-07:00","id":662777,"title":"","content":"Using American corporate metric, you would need <u>verified</u> signatures equal to 5x the projected (or actual) sales figures for the product in question to even open conversation about it. But White Wolf is a wholly-owned subsidiary of CCP, and Icelandic company, who handles licensing, so their criteria might be different. On top of that, licensing is usually contracted for a set amount of time, so even if you garnered the proper amount of signatures, it wouldn't help, as both parties may be locked into the contract for however many years. Even then, what would the financial alternative be? CCP licenses their WW IP's to companies that want to pay for them - By Night Studios was willing to pay. CCP reaps the profits of a third-party's work, and it would have to be a much sweeter stake for them to consider canceling their license. The decision between making some money for little to no work versus not making any money at all is not a hard one.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T02:06:33-07:00","id":662826,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#ff0000\">Rule #9 of the ToU comes into play here. What BNS does with their license is their's and CCP's business, not ours and we don't approve of posts like this or the potential cross site drama it could create. You also placed it in the wrong forum. I'm locking this down to further comment, do not create another topic about this subject.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"ty